<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tepanec War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1428">1428</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanec</a> War was the conflict of 1428 in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcoco">Texcoco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlacopan">Tlacopan</a>, overthrew the dominant Tepanec state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azcapotzalco">Azcapotzalco</a>. It followed the death of the Tepanec ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tezozomoc">Tezozomoc</a> and the succession struggle that ensued under his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maxtla">Maxtla</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> treat the victory as the founding moment of the empire and of the Triple Alliance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tepanec-war.jpg" alt="Tepanec War" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Aztec Empire (orthographic projection).svg : Keepscases Derivative work : Giggette · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aztec_Empire_ME_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
